@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] kit-one-engine-for-every-host
Claude Code and Codex sign-in, status, runs, model lists and efforts, and Gemini embeddings, MUST
live here once and be used by both Pully (`backend/`) and ThyMind, rather than copied into either.
A host MUST configure the kit once with its own names (`Config`: volume, container prefix, lock
file, environment prefix, image, container marker, sign-in hints, tools, extra secrets,
answer preparations), and the kit MUST NOT hard-code a host's volume, container, image, marker or
hint outside its tests. A host MUST NOT change its `volume` or `lock_file` once people have
signed in, because their sign-ins live there. Source: Tavi, 28 Oct 2026 ("make it a separate
package, which then you'll use for this too ... changes it to use this new shared package").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] kit-subscription-sign-in-only
The kit MUST run Claude Code and Codex only on a person's own subscription sign-in (claude.ai,
ChatGPT), each login in its own volume or container, and MUST NOT give either CLI an API key
(ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY) on any path. A sign-in MUST run the
unmodified CLI's own login (`claude auth login --claudeai`, `codex login --device-auth`) with
only that login's home, no job inputs, tools or prompt; the kit MUST NOT read the resulting
tokens and passes the person's pasted code only to that CLI's stdin. A phone MUST be given only
links on the providers' own sign-in hosts, and status MUST count only subscription sign-ins.
Source: backend `ai-runs-on-the-callers-own-sign-in` and `ai-sign-in-is-the-clis-own` (Tavi,
23 Oct 2026 13:39).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] kit-jobs-fail-closed
On a native server every CLI process MUST run in Docker with only its job folder read-write and
MUST fail rather than run on the host. The hosted agent container is itself the sandbox: there
the runner MUST refuse to start without the host's container marker, MUST run jobs as a user
that cannot read the login homes, and MUST refuse every login but its container's. A job MUST
get only the selected sign-in files of its login, never unrelated CLI settings or skills. Every
Codex job MUST disable `shell_tool`, `unified_exec` and `view_image`, whether or not the host
gives it tools. Stopping a run MUST kill its container or process. Source: backend
`server-every-cli-through-start-agent`, `rust-ai-capabilities-fail-closed`,
`rust-container-tools-use-scoped-capabilities`, `jobs-codex-pr-tools-only`; packages/worker
`hosted-ai-in-the-logins-own-container`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] kit-jobs-settle-and-clean-up
A job that acquired a concurrency slot MUST release it and settle even when its folder cannot be
made, and its timeout MUST exclude queue time. Cleanup MUST stop model and bootstrap containers
before the final sign-in files are saved, then retry removing named containers. Source: backend
`jobs-release-acquired-slots` and `rust-final-login-helper-is-cleaned`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] kit-secrets-never-leave
Model output, streamed activity, previews and errors MUST pass through `redact` before they reach
a host's caller. Any environment value whose name says TOKEN, KEY, SECRET or PASSWORD is redacted
where it appears, and the provider keys plus the host's own `Config::secrets` are redacted
whatever their length. Source: root `secrets-come-from-the-environment`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] kit-structured-answers-fit-their-schema
A structured answer MUST be checked against the schema the caller asked for before the caller
sees it: Codex gets the strict form of the schema and its nulls are dropped first, and a host
preparation runs only when the host named it in `Config::preparations`. Source: backend
`native-rpc-honors-declared-schemas` and `server-agent-results-checked`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] kit-builds-for-workers
The kit MUST build for `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with `agents` and `embed`, so a host can run in a
Cloudflare Worker. Its code MUST use `rt` for tasks, timers, environment, files and programs,
which fail closed in a Worker. `runner` is native only. Source: backend `server-builds-for-workers`.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] kit-embeddings-match-stored-vectors
`embed` MUST do no I/O: the host sends the request with its own client and key. Its text formats
(`title: … | text: …`, `task: search result | query: …`), JavaScript whitespace and UTF-16
clipping, the `f32` cast and the V8 `Math.hypot` normalisation MUST stay exactly as ThyMind's
stored vectors were made (ThyMind's port of `lib/ai.mjs`), or a search compares two spaces.
Changing any of them MUST re-embed every stored card in the same change. Source: Tavi, 28 Oct
2026 ("combining it with the stuff you have here, which is more of an embedding thing").
